  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef numpy_norm_gate(X: list, W: list, threshold: float = 2.0) -> list:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Norm-Gated Linear Transform** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef numpy_norm_gate(X: list, W: list, threshold: float = 2.0) -> list:\n    Z = np.dot(np.array(X, dtype=np.float64), np.array(W, dtype=np.float64))\n    Z[np.linalg.norm(Z, axis=1) < float(threshold)] = 0.0\n    return np.round(Z, 6).tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
